#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# region_bounds

#% text
# `region_bounds(reg)` gives the ranges `[[xmin, xmax], [ymin, ymax], ...]` of the region's coordinates.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Implicit and parametric regions are bounded numerically, by sampling and bisection.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A triangle:

#% cell
region_bounds(triangle([[0, 0], [1, 2], [2, 1]]))
#% output
#= [[0, 2], [0, 2]]

#% text
# A disk:

#% cell
region_bounds(disk([1, 2], 3))
#% output
#= [[-2, 4], [-1, 5]]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# An implicit region:

#% cell
region_bounds(implicit_region(x^2 + 4*y^2 <= 4, [x, y]))
#% output
#= [[-2.0, 2.0], [-1.0, 1.0]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `region_centroid`, `is_bounded_region`
